# An arm of a building `if` that ends on a widget taking a building `if`'s late plain
# result, the giver below the taker's `if` in the outer block, so the taker's result is
# the arm's own result and no name binds it (Semantics ch. 4, "Binding groups and
# cycles": any line may use any name the block binds, and the order of a group's lines
# decides positions and nothing else; ruling TC: places are counted as they are built).
# The closest program found to `DeferredLine`'s refusal "a line that takes a late result
# at its build, above the line that gives it, and gives a plain result of its own that no
# name binds (a pattern's, or the block's own result)"; on prismc-r27 it stops earlier,
# at the internal error "a prismc bug: the name n, which nothing declares".
# Written by Claude (t2, the prismc run), 12 November 2026; subject to change.
emit Ui.*
test mod Tests
use Ui.*

@Twice: fn Nat -> @Nat
fn @Twice k:
    Ui.Label($text=$"twice {k}")
    @ k * 2

@Seven: @Nat
@Seven:
    Ui.Label($text=$"seven")
    @ 7

@Page: fn Bool -> @unit
fn @Page loud:
    m <- if loud:
        Ui.Label($text=$"arm")                                         # 0
        @Twice n                                                       # 1
    else:
        @ 1
    Ui.Label($text=$"m {m}")                                           # 2, or 0
    n <- if loud:
        k <- @Seven                                                    # 3
        @ k
    else:
        @ 20
